      "Language": "ger",
      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": "The differential diagnosis of recently acquired cough, diarrhea, headaches, odynophagia and fever in AIDS-Patients is discussed. The aim is to find the most frequent, the treatable and the most dangerous diseases. We discuss the empirical and the symptomatic treatment in special situations."},
